  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "glib-networking security update",
      "Title": "Synopsis",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for glib-networking is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP4",
      "Title": "Summary",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "glib-networking contains the implementations of certain GLib networking features that cannot be implemented directly in GLib itself because of their dependencies.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA flaw was found in glib-networking. When establishing connections using Transport Layer Security (TLS) version 1.3, the client-side session cache does not limit the number of session tickets retained for a single host. A malicious server can exploit this by sending excessive session ticket messages, causing the client application to continuously consume memory. This unbounded memory growth can exhaust system memory, resulting in a Denial of Service (DoS).(CVE-2026-103963)",
      "Title": "Description",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for glib-networking is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP4.\n\nopenEuler Security has rated this update as having a security impact of high. A Common Vunlnerability Scoring System(CVSS)base score,which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVElink(s) in the References section.",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "High",
      "Title": "Severity",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "glib-networking",
      "Title": "Affected Component",
      "Type": "General"
    }
  ],
